00:16:06.536 --> 00:16:09.596
BRITT: That's it.
BREE: Ow! Mom!


00:16:11.608 --> 00:16:13.269
Have another crab puff, Rod.


00:16:14.044 --> 00:16:17.138
Mom, he's hungry. It's been 40 minutes.


00:16:17.781 --> 00:16:20.409
Look, you asked me to come, I'm here.


00:16:20.584 --> 00:16:24.020
- But five more minutes and I'm out.
- I'm right behind you, JP.


00:16:26.690 --> 00:16:30.148
Joey, I know that you and Dominique
have had your differences...


00:16:30.327 --> 00:16:33.763
...but try not to bring up
the time she dissed you on <i>TRL.</i>


00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:34.954
She didn't mean it.


00:16:35.132 --> 00:16:37.999
How do you call someone overrated
and not mean it? That's just disrespect.


00:16:38.168 --> 00:16:39.260
Shh.


00:16:41.004 --> 00:16:45.407
Joey, doing a duet with Dominique
means reaching her audience.


00:16:45.575 --> 00:16:47.008
Like Daddy and I.


00:16:47.477 --> 00:16:49.411
And if doing a duet means that Mommy...


00:16:51.214 --> 00:16:55.344
- The family can have another house, well...
- Okay, Mom, you have a house.


00:16:55.619 --> 00:16:56.643
Okay?


00:16:56.820 --> 00:16:59.789
Nobody's bought a Dominique CD
in years. I mean, she's not cool.


00:16:59.956 --> 00:17:00.980
I think she's cool.


00:17:02.059 --> 00:17:03.959
Thank you. Exactly.


00:17:04.127 --> 00:17:05.617
DOMINIQUE:
Hi.


00:17:06.530 --> 00:17:11.126
Look at all of these beautiful people.


00:17:11.301 --> 00:17:13.428
Well, I'm so sorry
to keep you all waiting.


00:17:13.603 --> 00:17:17.004
But it took 20 minutes
to descend the staircase.


00:17:17.174 --> 00:17:19.642
But it was worth it, don't you think?


00:17:19.976 --> 00:17:21.500
Hello, Rod. No, no.


00:17:21.678 --> 00:17:23.976
Evie. No, no, no.


00:17:24.147 --> 00:17:26.342
- Young man whose name I don't know.
- I'm...


00:17:26.516 --> 00:17:27.710
Oh. Shh.


00:17:27.884 --> 00:17:29.852
ROD:
Wow, that's some dress.


00:17:30.020 --> 00:17:33.114
Oh, yeah?
I'm wearing this in my next video.


00:17:33.290 --> 00:17:36.225
It's a duet, great stuff.


00:17:36.393 --> 00:17:38.486
Hello, Grammy. Ha-ha-ha.


00:17:38.662 --> 00:17:39.686
[LAUGHING]


00:17:39.863 --> 00:17:42.195
But enough about me, for now.


00:17:43.100 --> 00:17:44.795
ROD:
Oh, let me help you.


00:17:44.968 --> 00:17:46.196
- Yeah. Um...
DOMINIQUE: Thank you.


00:17:46.369 --> 00:17:48.234
Look, Dominique...


00:17:49.406 --> 00:17:52.307
...I'm not doing the duet with you, okay?


00:17:52.476 --> 00:17:54.137
No, listen to what she has to say.


00:17:54.311 --> 00:17:55.642
DOMINIQUE: Zip it, Rod.
ROD: Or not.


00:17:55.812 --> 00:17:57.837
Drinks, we need drinks. Mary?


00:17:58.381 --> 00:18:00.144
Well, thanks, but I don't drink.


00:18:00.317 --> 00:18:02.979
- Oh, my God.
JOEY: Sorry. Thank you.


00:18:03.353 --> 00:18:05.719
Of course you don't, darling boy,
but I do.


00:18:05.889 --> 00:18:07.686
- Okay.
- I drink.


00:18:07.958 --> 00:18:09.255
- So, Joey...
- I'll get you one.


00:18:09.426 --> 00:18:11.485
...asked anyone
to the Black and White Ball yet?


00:18:11.661 --> 00:18:13.856
You have a crab puff in your teeth, Britt.


00:18:14.030 --> 00:18:16.191
- You should really take me to the ball.
- Yeah.


00:18:16.366 --> 00:18:19.199
I speak French. How about you?


00:18:19.369 --> 00:18:20.631
Thanks, yeah.


00:18:20.804 --> 00:18:24.296
Look, Dominique, I'm kind of on a break
right now, so...


00:18:24.474 --> 00:18:27.932
You all must be famished.
First course, Mary. Now.


00:18:28.678 --> 00:18:32.114
Joey would gladly take a break
from his break.


00:18:32.282 --> 00:18:35.080
No. No, no.
Actually, I am focusing on school.


00:18:35.252 --> 00:18:39.211
- I'm just hanging with friends, you know?
- That's right. The new JP.


00:18:39.389 --> 00:18:40.617
Who are you?


00:18:40.791 --> 00:18:42.258
I'm Joey Parker's manager.


00:18:42.425 --> 00:18:45.121
Oh, please ignore him.


00:18:45.295 --> 00:18:46.922
I'm Joey's manager.


00:18:47.097 --> 00:18:48.758
BRITT:
You have two managers?


00:18:48.932 --> 00:18:51.594
- Apparently.
- You must be a real handful.


00:18:51.768 --> 00:18:53.201
Wanna make out?


00:18:53.370 --> 00:18:55.235
You know, actually, technically, I'm...


00:18:55.405 --> 00:18:58.704
Oh, shut up, Rod. Even I know
you're completely inconsequential.


00:18:58.875 --> 00:19:00.433
You see? It's not just me.


00:19:00.610 --> 00:19:02.771
JOEY:
This is why I did not wanna come today.


00:19:03.647 --> 00:19:04.875
You're all nuts.


00:19:05.282 --> 00:19:09.150
You can either do the duet with me
and become a superstar...


00:19:09.319 --> 00:19:14.052
...or you can fade away
into teenybopper obscurity.


00:19:14.224 --> 00:19:16.954
Okay. I've heard enough, okay?


00:19:17.127 --> 00:19:19.595
Joey Parker is a man
that needs to do things his way.


00:19:19.763 --> 00:19:24.826
He needs to keep it real. So from here
on out, I'm Joey Parker's only manager.


00:19:25.001 --> 00:19:26.525
I think we're done here. Let's go.


00:19:26.703 --> 00:19:28.000
Thanks for everything.


00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:33.632
We keep meeting like this.


00:19:33.810 --> 00:19:36.438
You have shrimp in your hair.


00:19:36.613 --> 00:19:37.739
DUSTIN:
Come on.


00:19:37.914 --> 00:19:39.245
- You all right?
EVIE: That's nuts.


00:19:39.416 --> 00:19:41.281
- You hear how he...?
ROD: I don't care!


00:19:41.451 --> 00:19:43.078
DUSTIN: Are you ready?
- Mary?


00:19:43.253 --> 00:19:44.277
DUSTIN:
Let's go.


00:19:44.454 --> 00:19:49.323
You will clean this room spotless
in 30 minutes. Rod.


00:19:50.961 --> 00:19:54.419
And your phone privileges are suspended
for an entire month. Cough it up.


00:19:54.598 --> 00:19:55.963
Come on, look alive.


00:19:56.499 --> 00:19:58.467
Clean.


00:19:58.635 --> 00:20:00.364
Joey, honey, wait.


00:20:00.537 --> 00:20:02.596
I gotta talk to you.


00:20:08.278 --> 00:20:09.939
Tami, don't hate me...


00:20:11.948 --> 00:20:13.939
...but I don't wanna go to the ball.


00:20:14.117 --> 00:20:17.052
You have to go. I've been working
on our dresses for two weeks.


00:20:17.220 --> 00:20:19.415
I know. I know. It's just...


00:20:19.589 --> 00:20:23.116
I don't know. It's on Valentine's Day.
We don't even have dates.


00:20:23.293 --> 00:20:26.194
Plus, everyone's gonna be wearing masks,
which is really weird.


00:20:26.363 --> 00:20:30.129
But that's good. We can each meet
a handsome, mysterious stranger.


00:20:30.400 --> 00:20:32.868
How will we know he's handsome
if he's wearing a mask?


00:20:33.036 --> 00:20:35.561
By how he dances.
Hot guys always dance the best.


00:20:35.739 --> 00:20:37.263
- Anyway...
- I don't fit in here.


00:20:37.440 --> 00:20:39.806
So why go and pretend like I do?


00:20:39.976 --> 00:20:41.409
Guys don't even know I exist.


00:20:41.578 --> 00:20:44.138
Again, no one will know who anyone is.


00:20:44.314 --> 00:20:46.680
There's no such thing as not fitting in.


00:20:46.850 --> 00:20:49.182
If there's a guy you like,
he'll meet the real you.


00:20:49.352 --> 00:20:53.152
Not some fake you that's been created
by the cliques at our lame-ass high school.


00:20:53.323 --> 00:20:55.314
- Don't get me started about... What?
- Tami.


00:20:55.492 --> 00:20:58.120
You should really breathe
in between monologues.


00:20:58.295 --> 00:20:59.922
You're going to the ball.


00:21:01.231 --> 00:21:02.926
Oh, I forgot to start cleaning.


00:21:03.767 --> 00:21:05.632
DOMINIQUE:
<i>Faster.</i>


00:21:07.137 --> 00:21:09.332
Give it a rhythm. Make it a samba.


00:21:09.506 --> 00:21:10.666
Give it a:


00:21:10.840 --> 00:21:12.364
[HUMMING]


00:21:14.477 --> 00:21:15.774
- Mother.
- Mommy?


00:21:15.946 --> 00:21:17.413
Hello, my little pretties.


00:21:17.580 --> 00:21:21.641
This is Fabio and Paulo
and somebody else.


00:21:21.818 --> 00:21:24.912
I'm thinking of making one of them
my new daddy.


00:21:25.488 --> 00:21:27.422
I mean, your new daddy.


00:21:27.590 --> 00:21:29.581
Anyway, uh...


00:21:29.759 --> 00:21:32.819
...we were on our way to get manis
and pedis for the ball tonight.


00:21:32.996 --> 00:21:36.432
Which we heard Mary talking about, FYI.


00:21:36.599 --> 00:21:39.295
As in she's planning to go, FYI.


00:21:40.070 --> 00:21:41.401
Oh. Oh...


00:21:41.571 --> 00:21:43.436
That won't do.


00:21:44.374 --> 00:21:46.706
Uh, you could tell her to clean my room.


00:21:46.876 --> 00:21:49.037
And my closet.
I think something died in there.


00:21:49.212 --> 00:21:51.009
No, no, no.


00:21:51.181 --> 00:21:56.949
I have a very special place
that needs cleaning.


00:21:58.788 --> 00:21:59.948
DOMINIQUE:
Mary?


00:22:01.524 --> 00:22:05.221
- The twins are turning 16 next week.
- Didn't they turn 16 last year?


00:22:05.595 --> 00:22:09.361
Yes, and they'll keep turning 16
until I tell them to stop.


00:22:09.532 --> 00:22:13.525
We're having a big party
and I need this house to be spotless.


00:22:13.703 --> 00:22:17.969
But Tami and I are going to the ball.
Plus, I've cleaned every room in this house.


00:22:18.141 --> 00:22:19.733
Not...


00:22:21.244 --> 00:22:23.007
...my bedroom.


00:22:28.151 --> 00:22:30.517
You're kidding me, right?


00:22:31.354 --> 00:22:32.821
I'm clubbing with Paris tonight.


00:22:32.989 --> 00:22:36.652
It's my turn to throw the after-party.
Don't step on my hair.


00:22:36.826 --> 00:22:41.695
When I get home at midnight,
this room will be pristine.


00:22:41.865 --> 00:22:45.198
Dominique, I'd need heavy equipment.
For example, a flamethrower.


00:22:45.568 --> 00:22:48.867
Don't you sass me, smarty pants.


00:22:49.039 --> 00:22:51.098
I'll revoke your school privileges.


00:22:51.274 --> 00:22:53.504
You could say goodbye
to those trendy friends.


00:22:53.676 --> 00:22:59.114
Or shall I say friend,
Little Miss Not-So-Popular?


00:22:59.282 --> 00:23:00.306
[CHUCKLES]


00:23:01.351 --> 00:23:02.375
Ooh!


00:23:03.086 --> 00:23:06.385
Oh, and clean up these fish sticks.
They've been there since Lent.


00:23:10.627 --> 00:23:11.992
[PHONE RINGS]


00:23:12.929 --> 00:23:14.362
MARY:
<i>Tami, I can't go to the ball.</i>


00:23:14.531 --> 00:23:16.465
"Domifreak's" making me clean
her bedroom.


00:23:17.000 --> 00:23:18.968
You're in her lair?


00:23:19.135 --> 00:23:22.229
There are species of bugs in here
still unknown to science.


00:23:22.405 --> 00:23:24.805
<i>There's no way I'll finish in time.</i>


00:23:25.275 --> 00:23:27.243
- Wait, what if...?
DOMINIQUE: <i>Who are you talking to?</i>


00:23:27.744 --> 00:23:31.077
<i>When I said no phone privileges,</i>
<i>that included the landline.</i>


00:23:31.247 --> 00:23:32.805
I'm sorry. I have to go.


00:23:41.658 --> 00:23:43.023
Ugh.


00:23:57.540 --> 00:23:58.871
[RUSTLING]


00:24:13.656 --> 00:24:14.987
[GROWLING]


00:24:18.194 --> 00:24:19.525
[BARKING]


00:24:19.696 --> 00:24:23.860
Manson, we've been looking for you
since Christmas, boy.


00:24:24.033 --> 00:24:26.024
You're free, boy. Go. Go, go.


00:24:28.872 --> 00:24:30.362
[DOORBELL RINGS]


00:24:33.276 --> 00:24:35.471
Go, Manson, go. You're free. Oh, hey.


00:24:35.645 --> 00:24:39.274
Gosh, look, I just found Manson.
And please tell me those aren't our dresses.


00:24:39.682 --> 00:24:42.310
I can't. Because they are.


00:24:42.485 --> 00:24:44.146
We're going to the ball.


00:24:44.320 --> 00:24:48.222
Tami, what part of "Domifreak's making me
clean her bedroom" did you not understand?


00:24:48.791 --> 00:24:52.192
What would you say if I told you
I could clean up the mess for you...


00:24:52.362 --> 00:24:54.455
...and Dominique would never know?


00:24:54.631 --> 00:24:58.397
I'd say you're my hero, but there's no way,
and you have to go to the ball.


00:24:58.568 --> 00:25:03.164
- Plus, you can't clean this mess up alone.
- Well, who said I was alone?


00:25:04.474 --> 00:25:05.498
- Hi, Mary.
- Hey.


00:25:06.142 --> 00:25:07.507
You did this for me?


00:25:07.677 --> 00:25:10.407
Mary, meet my sister's
boyfriend's cousins.


00:25:10.580 --> 00:25:13.048
Cousins, this is Mary.


00:25:13.216 --> 00:25:15.411
Hello, hello. You go to dance?


00:25:15.585 --> 00:25:16.847
Very nice.


00:25:17.020 --> 00:25:18.248
House clean by midnight?


00:25:18.421 --> 00:25:23.154
No problem. Like van say, "No mess...


00:25:23.326 --> 00:25:25.590
...too messy."
- Okay.


00:25:28.164 --> 00:25:29.722
This mess is too messy.


00:25:29.899 --> 00:25:32.424
- Lee-Ha, you promised.
- Is there a problem?


00:25:32.602 --> 00:25:35.537
I'm on it. Get started and hide the van.


00:25:37.574 --> 00:25:39.565
[MUSIC PLAYING]


00:25:39.742 --> 00:25:40.868
BREE:
Isn't that him?


00:25:41.044 --> 00:25:44.411
No, that's not him.
Oh, that's him. No, it's not.


00:25:45.548 --> 00:25:47.072
Joey can dance.


00:25:47.250 --> 00:25:49.684
When we see a guy who can move,
we'll have our man.


00:25:49.852 --> 00:25:51.945
Let me know when you find him.


00:25:52.121 --> 00:25:55.056
Hey, we were just looking for you.


00:25:55.225 --> 00:25:58.023
Yeah, I'm sure you were.


00:25:59.295 --> 00:26:01.627
- Nice mask.
- Nice dress.


00:26:01.798 --> 00:26:03.789
Nice face.


00:26:05.535 --> 00:26:07.298
Hey, ladies, hey.


00:26:07.470 --> 00:26:10.462
Boo, where you going?
All the funk you need is right here.


00:26:10.640 --> 00:26:11.971
[CHUCKLES]


00:26:13.576 --> 00:26:15.203
Man.


00:26:15.645 --> 00:26:16.907
Hey, man.


00:26:17.080 --> 00:26:19.275
Why did you tell me this
was a costume party?


00:26:19.449 --> 00:26:20.882
It is the Black and White Ball.


00:26:21.050 --> 00:26:22.642
You look good, man. This is sharp.


00:26:22.819 --> 00:26:24.844
I do clean up good, huh?


00:26:26.055 --> 00:26:28.489
I guess I'm not the only one
who didn't get the memo.


00:26:30.660 --> 00:26:33.493
- Who is that?
- No idea.


00:26:34.664 --> 00:26:36.097
But I'm gonna find out.


00:26:36.532 --> 00:26:37.931
Everyone's looking at me.


00:26:38.101 --> 00:26:41.002
Who's the Lohan
who decided to make her own rules?


00:26:41.170 --> 00:26:43.229
You need a drink.
Punch bowl, straight ahead.


00:26:43.406 --> 00:26:46.842
I don't know, but she looks good.


00:26:47.510 --> 00:26:51.844
I mean, not good like us. Good like bad.
Pff.


00:26:53.182 --> 00:26:55.946
DUSTIN: Here they come.
- All right, be cool. Be cool.


00:27:01.524 --> 00:27:03.253
JOEY:
Hi.


00:27:03.693 --> 00:27:07.527
You really know how to make an entrance.
That, uh, dress is amazing.


00:27:08.598 --> 00:27:11.533
Thank you. That's a nice cape.


00:27:13.136 --> 00:27:15.536
I mean, coat. It's a nice coat...


00:27:15.838 --> 00:27:18.033
- What should I do?
- Say something. Anything.


00:27:18.207 --> 00:27:19.936
- He's cute.
- Um...


00:27:20.109 --> 00:27:22.669
Hey, do you want some punch?


00:27:23.112 --> 00:27:24.875
Or you have some... Cool, okay.


00:27:31.788 --> 00:27:32.948
Weird.


00:27:33.122 --> 00:27:35.488
- Are you supposed to be Cupid?
- Yeah. Smart girl.


00:27:36.059 --> 00:27:37.117
Dope, right?


00:27:37.293 --> 00:27:40.558
With these arrows of love,
somebody gonna fall hard tonight.


00:27:40.730 --> 00:27:43.062
- Is that so?
- Yeah.


00:27:43.232 --> 00:27:45.427
Usually, I'm a lot cooler than this.


00:27:45.601 --> 00:27:48.399
I'm actually, like,
Joey Parker's best friend, see?


00:27:48.571 --> 00:27:51.699
- Is that supposed to impress me?
- Yeah, a little.


00:27:52.141 --> 00:27:54.166
You wanna see my Cupid dance?


00:28:04.554 --> 00:28:07.250
- What was that?
- I don't usually come to these things.


00:28:07.423 --> 00:28:08.720
Yeah, me too.


00:28:08.891 --> 00:28:11.257
What? Wait. Do you, um, wanna...?


00:28:11.427 --> 00:28:13.190
Wait. You don't like to dance?


00:28:13.363 --> 00:28:14.591
Sorry, what?


00:28:15.264 --> 00:28:17.095
- Do you wanna...?
- Hey.


00:28:17.266 --> 00:28:18.927
Can I ask you to dance?


00:28:20.470 --> 00:28:22.529
Yes, I'd love to.


00:28:27.443 --> 00:28:29.172
Now, don't take this the wrong way...


00:28:29.345 --> 00:28:32.075
...but I have never seen anything like you
in my life.


00:28:32.248 --> 00:28:34.148
- That's a good thing, right?
- Yes.


00:28:34.317 --> 00:28:35.841
Dance with me, Cupid-man.


00:28:40.356 --> 00:28:43.519
Do me a favor. Can you play this for me?
Track five.


00:28:43.693 --> 00:28:45.661
Here, hold this for me.


00:28:45.828 --> 00:28:46.817
Hey.


00:28:46.996 --> 00:28:48.020
[TANGO MUSIC PLAYING]


00:28:48.197 --> 00:28:50.256
GIRL:
Shake it, baby.


00:28:50.666 --> 00:28:51.690
Nice.


00:29:03.413 --> 00:29:06.541
- What was that?
- I guess the music just speaks to me.


00:29:12.789 --> 00:29:15.189
Well, I guess
we don't have a language barrier.


00:29:16.559 --> 00:29:19.960
Isn't that funny? I just love monkeys too.
Anyway, she'd...


00:29:21.864 --> 00:29:23.456
Look at him move.


00:29:23.633 --> 00:29:25.260
That has to be Joey.


00:29:25.435 --> 00:29:27.562
But who's the tramp?


00:29:50.159 --> 00:29:51.183
[CROWD CHEERING]


00:29:51.894 --> 00:29:52.918
Ow.


00:30:20.156 --> 00:30:21.384
[CHUCKLING]


00:30:32.368 --> 00:30:33.494
Oh...


00:30:33.669 --> 00:30:35.330
Oh, hey, are you okay?


00:30:38.407 --> 00:30:39.567
You were amazing.


00:30:39.742 --> 00:30:41.733
No, I wasn't. I fell.


00:30:45.381 --> 00:30:46.405
Joey?


00:30:48.084 --> 00:30:49.108
[CLOCK CHIMING]


00:30:51.921 --> 00:30:53.650
I have to go.


00:30:55.091 --> 00:30:56.991
I have to go. Can I have it back?


00:30:57.159 --> 00:30:59.525
- Today?
GIRL: Is that Joey?


00:30:59.695 --> 00:31:01.162
Wait, wait...


00:31:01.330 --> 00:31:02.820
- I'm late.
- Where are you...?


00:31:03.666 --> 00:31:05.065
JOEY:
Wait.


00:31:12.141 --> 00:31:13.733
MARY:
Oh, my God. That was...


00:31:13.910 --> 00:31:16.879
TAMI: Holy cow...
- I feel like I have to throw up.


00:31:17.046 --> 00:31:19.708
Tami, if I don't get home by midnight,
I am dead.


00:31:19.882 --> 00:31:21.941
You were dancing with Joey Parker.


00:31:22.118 --> 00:31:25.349
I fell on my butt with Joey Parker.
God, I knew I shouldn't have come.


00:31:25.521 --> 00:31:29.355
- He was into you.
- Because he didn't know who I was.


00:31:29.625 --> 00:31:31.115
You really think he was into me?


00:31:31.294 --> 00:31:32.955
[TRANSMISSION GRINDING]


00:31:36.732 --> 00:31:37.790
[ENGINE RATTLING]


00:31:40.469 --> 00:31:44.235
- I'm so sorry.
- No, no, no, this can't be happening.


00:31:51.814 --> 00:31:53.805
[SPEAKING IN CHINESE]


00:32:01.457 --> 00:32:02.788
[GASPS]


00:32:09.532 --> 00:32:13.491
I am not doing
that old diva's talk show again.


00:32:14.270 --> 00:32:15.669
She's got a serious... What?


00:32:16.739 --> 00:32:18.070
Oh, God.


00:32:18.240 --> 00:32:22.506
She's got a serious case
of the grab-hands.


00:32:24.213 --> 00:32:27.046
No, no, no, she's right behind me.
Go, go, go.


00:32:30.486 --> 00:32:32.147
No, no, no!


00:32:32.321 --> 00:32:35.256
That's my answer
to all those talk shows. No!


00:32:40.029 --> 00:32:42.623
Go that way, that way, that way. Go.


00:32:49.405 --> 00:32:52.203
Hmm. Well, it seems you managed
to follow orders.


00:32:52.742 --> 00:32:53.868
For once.


00:32:54.777 --> 00:32:56.802
Why are you wearing my robe?


00:32:57.179 --> 00:33:00.376
I was admiring its silky quality.


00:33:03.619 --> 00:33:08.147
You like my after-party?
It's a total rager, isn't it? Ha-ha.


00:33:08.591 --> 00:33:11.219
Oh, it's not a rager at all.


00:33:11.394 --> 00:33:13.487
No one's coming.


00:33:13.763 --> 00:33:17.722
I'm a Little Miss Not-So-Popular too.


00:33:18.734 --> 00:33:21.703
God, I'm so tired.


00:33:28.210 --> 00:33:30.007
[MOUTHS]
<i>Thank you.</i>


00:33:34.684 --> 00:33:39.314
All right, now, look. If you pull this off,
you will be the prince of all princes, okay?


00:33:39.488 --> 00:33:43.015
- Now, just let me talk to the teacher.
- Why aren't you two in class?


00:33:45.761 --> 00:33:48.161
I have a huge favor to ask, Miss B.


00:33:48.330 --> 00:33:50.890
I need to find somebody
who was at the dance last night.


00:33:51.067 --> 00:33:52.932
And if you don't, you'll die?


00:33:54.470 --> 00:33:56.097
I think I might.


00:33:57.873 --> 00:33:59.773
GIRL: No way.
BOY: Yeah.


00:33:59.942 --> 00:34:02.604
Whoever she was, she was a freak show.


00:34:02.778 --> 00:34:05.611
Totally.
Who runs away from Joey Parker?


00:34:05.781 --> 00:34:07.043
Not me.


00:34:07.216 --> 00:34:09.013
She'll never show her face now.


00:34:12.254 --> 00:34:14.017
We missed you at the ball, Mary.


00:34:14.190 --> 00:34:17.125
I guess a maid's job is just never done.


00:34:18.427 --> 00:34:20.292
[PA CHIMES]


00:34:20.763 --> 00:34:24.426
This is an administrative announcement
from the administrative office.


00:34:24.600 --> 00:34:26.090
[LAUGHING]


00:34:27.002 --> 00:34:28.196
What's up?


00:34:28.370 --> 00:34:30.565
You're on the mike
with the Funk master.


00:34:30.740 --> 00:34:32.173
[LAUGHING]


00:34:32.341 --> 00:34:36.141
- Okay, very funny. Keep the voices down.
- <i>Check it out. Listen up.</i>


00:34:36.312 --> 00:34:38.644
[RAPPING] <i>Once upon a time</i>
<i>There was this chill hottie</i>


00:34:38.814 --> 00:34:41.214
<i>She left Joey Parker</i>
<i>Now, that was real naughty</i>


00:34:41.383 --> 00:34:43.374
<i>Now here's JP just to tell you more</i>


00:34:43.552 --> 00:34:45.986
<i>Now, put down your pencils</i>
<i>And give JP the floor</i>


00:34:46.155 --> 00:34:47.816
All right, Funk, Funk, that's good.


00:34:47.990 --> 00:34:49.321
[DUSTIN]
<i>'Cause I was on the mike...</i>


00:34:49.492 --> 00:34:51.926
- All right, I got another verse.
- Funk, thank you.


00:34:52.094 --> 00:34:54.756
- You're welcome.
- That was the Funk, ladies and gentlemen.


00:34:54.930 --> 00:34:56.227
<i>Anyway...</i>


00:34:56.398 --> 00:34:59.492
...last night, I, uh...
I danced with somebody at the ball.


00:35:00.035 --> 00:35:02.333
<i>And you dropped your Zune</i>
<i>when you left.</i>


00:35:02.505 --> 00:35:05.804
<i>I'd love to return it.</i>
<i>The problem is, I don't know who you are.</i>


00:35:06.275 --> 00:35:07.936
And this is important...


00:35:08.110 --> 00:35:11.944
<i>... because you made</i>
<i>it one of the best nights of my life.</i>


00:35:12.248 --> 00:35:13.272
I...


00:35:13.449 --> 00:35:15.110
...love him.


00:35:15.284 --> 00:35:18.014
You have bacon in your braces.


00:35:18.187 --> 00:35:19.848
Keep the voices down.


00:35:21.257 --> 00:35:23.452
Okay, so here's the deal. Uh...


00:35:23.626 --> 00:35:26.220
If you were the girl
that I danced with last night...


00:35:26.395 --> 00:35:30.456
<i>... tell me the names of the four</i>
<i>most-listened-to songs on your playlist.</i>


00:35:30.633 --> 00:35:31.861
Thanks, mystery girl.


00:35:32.034 --> 00:35:33.262
<i>I'll be waiting.</i>


00:35:33.435 --> 00:35:36.165
"Thanks, mystery girl. I'll be waiting."


00:35:39.542 --> 00:35:42.067
- That was good. That was good.
- Was that all right?


00:35:42.244 --> 00:35:43.871
This is gonna be easy.


00:35:44.046 --> 00:35:45.536
[SOBBING]


00:35:45.714 --> 00:35:50.276
I know. I know, sweetie.
It's okay, but you gotta go, okay? All right.


00:35:50.452 --> 00:35:52.784
Just... All right, yeah. Whoo.


00:35:52.955 --> 00:35:55.287
Everybody, please,
single-file line, all right?


00:35:55.457 --> 00:35:57.448
You guys are so not his mystery girl.


00:35:57.626 --> 00:36:00.060
All right, everybody's gonna get a chance
to meet JP.


00:36:00.229 --> 00:36:01.457
You call me. Ha-ha.


00:36:01.630 --> 00:36:04.360
All right, all right. Cynthia? It's your turn.


00:36:04.533 --> 00:36:05.795
- You ready?
- Yes.


00:36:05.968 --> 00:36:07.458
All right, good.


00:36:07.636 --> 00:36:09.263
Look excited.


00:36:09.805 --> 00:36:10.829
Hey.


00:36:11.006 --> 00:36:16.740
"Push," "High," "Boys Don't Cry,"
and "Lullaby," all by the Cure.


00:36:18.747 --> 00:36:20.908
Now give me my Zune.


00:36:21.851 --> 00:36:23.250
I'm sorry, that's not it.


00:36:23.853 --> 00:36:26.253
- All right, I'm sorry. It's okay.
- Get off.


00:36:27.823 --> 00:36:28.847
[SIGHS]


00:36:29.024 --> 00:36:30.321
Hey.


00:36:30.593 --> 00:36:32.561
Mind if I pick up the slack
you don't want?


00:36:32.728 --> 00:36:34.821
- Knock yourself out.
- I will.


00:36:36.098 --> 00:36:37.531
God, they're all the same.


00:36:38.534 --> 00:36:40.024
But that girl from last night.


00:36:40.603 --> 00:36:43.197
- Special.
- Yeah, man, I saw it, man.


00:36:43.639 --> 00:36:48.804
I mean, I haven't seen you dance like that
since the 2006 VMAs, remember that night?


00:36:48.978 --> 00:36:50.275
It's pretty funky.


00:36:50.446 --> 00:36:52.607
So look, we're gonna find her, all right?


00:36:53.282 --> 00:36:54.874
She's here somewhere.


00:36:55.284 --> 00:36:57.616
I think she helped you
get your mojo back.


00:36:57.786 --> 00:37:00.186
Yeah, you're with me.


00:37:00.356 --> 00:37:01.948
- Let's do it.
- Who's next?


00:37:02.124 --> 00:37:04.649
Come on, ladies, have your songs ready.


00:37:04.827 --> 00:37:06.920
Oh, my gosh. He wasn't kidding.


00:37:07.096 --> 00:37:10.031
Go down and tell him it was you
before someone starts a riot.


00:37:10.199 --> 00:37:11.223
Forget it, Tami.


00:37:11.400 --> 00:37:14.563
He said last night
was one of the best nights of his life.


00:37:14.737 --> 00:37:17.604
- Yeah.
- Until he finds out it was me.


00:37:19.708 --> 00:37:22.575
- Are you listening? Come on.
- No. What?


00:37:25.748 --> 00:37:27.613
BRITT:
Stop right there.


00:37:28.884 --> 00:37:32.376
Oh, look at you, acting all innocent.


00:37:32.554 --> 00:37:35.853
- What are you talking about?
BREE: We know, Mary.


00:37:36.025 --> 00:37:39.324
- What?
- It was you at the ball. With Joey.


00:37:41.096 --> 00:37:43.064
- You guys are crazy.
- No, you're crazy...


00:37:43.232 --> 00:37:46.463
...if you think we'll let you end up
with Joey, Miss Stalker Face.


00:37:46.635 --> 00:37:49.069
And if you tell him it was you...


00:37:49.238 --> 00:37:51.206
...this video will be everywhere.


00:37:51.373 --> 00:37:52.840
Hello, YouTube.


00:37:53.008 --> 00:37:56.000
You barely know how to work the toaster,
let alone YouTube.


00:37:56.178 --> 00:37:58.078
Well, try us.


00:37:58.814 --> 00:38:00.839
Now, go make the lamb chops.


00:38:01.016 --> 00:38:02.779
Mother's very hungry.


00:38:07.423 --> 00:38:08.913
Where are you going?


00:38:09.091 --> 00:38:12.527
None of your beeswax. I mean, nowhere.


00:38:12.695 --> 00:38:15.687
For a walk. In the woods.


00:38:17.032 --> 00:38:18.556
Okay.


00:38:19.401 --> 00:38:20.766
Ow! Oh...


00:38:24.406 --> 00:38:27.773
If I were a playlist,
where would I hide myself?


00:38:36.485 --> 00:38:38.851
In plain sight.


00:38:39.021 --> 00:38:40.454
Brilliant.


00:38:42.825 --> 00:38:45.885
"We All Fall Down."
"She Wants to Move."


00:38:51.467 --> 00:38:52.491
[BRITT GROANS]


00:39:03.345 --> 00:39:08.009
Do you think maybe you could give me
a clue as to what the songs are?


00:39:08.617 --> 00:39:10.278
Are they emo?


00:39:10.452 --> 00:39:12.113
Techno?


00:39:12.554 --> 00:39:13.885
Young contemporary?


00:39:14.056 --> 00:39:18.493
Okay, people, people.
Please, disperse, okay?


00:39:18.660 --> 00:39:19.922
He's gonna take a break...


00:39:20.095 --> 00:39:24.156
...and you guys can just come line up
after class or something, all right?


00:39:24.333 --> 00:39:27.029
- I'm never gonna find her.
- Hey, hey, hey, mister.


00:39:27.202 --> 00:39:30.535
I don't wanna hear that crazy talk.
You leave that in crazy town, okay?


00:39:30.706 --> 00:39:34.039
Remember, you're Joey Parker,
and Joey Parker always gets his girl.


00:39:34.209 --> 00:39:35.608
I'm right. You know I'm right.


00:39:36.011 --> 00:39:38.912
All right, what's your name? Say it, huh?


00:39:39.081 --> 00:39:41.242
- I'm...
- Joey Parker.


00:39:41.417 --> 00:39:43.783
Your prayers have been answered.


00:39:43.952 --> 00:39:45.351
Whoa, whoa, whoa.


00:39:46.221 --> 00:39:49.418
Look, Britt, okay?
Joey is on break, okay?


00:39:49.591 --> 00:39:50.990
And he's exhausted...


00:39:51.160 --> 00:39:53.424
Oh, I'm not here to talk to Joey.


00:39:53.595 --> 00:39:55.062
I'm in the mood for some funk.


00:39:57.166 --> 00:39:59.794
- Really?
- No. Now, get out of my way.


00:40:02.337 --> 00:40:05.397
I'm the one.


00:40:06.108 --> 00:40:07.132
[SCOFFS]


00:40:07.943 --> 00:40:10.070
You're kidding me, right?


00:40:10.245 --> 00:40:13.476
I can totally prove it.
I know all the songs on the Zune.


00:40:14.450 --> 00:40:15.883
Prove it.


00:40:16.618 --> 00:40:20.486
"We All Fall Down," "She Wants to Move,"
"Pon de Replay," and "Hips Don't Lie."


00:40:22.524 --> 00:40:23.821
I'm right, right?


00:40:24.526 --> 00:40:26.494
I knew it!


00:40:26.829 --> 00:40:29.195
Well, what are you waiting for?


00:40:29.565 --> 00:40:32.056
- Kiss me.
- No, no, no.


00:40:32.234 --> 00:40:33.496
We're gonna dance first.


00:40:33.669 --> 00:40:35.432
What?


00:40:36.338 --> 00:40:39.068
But you said we only needed
to know the songs.


00:40:39.241 --> 00:40:41.869
Plus, I'm not warmed up.
And there's no music.


00:40:42.044 --> 00:40:45.172
Well, if you were the one,
you wouldn't need music.


00:40:45.347 --> 00:40:47.247
- Sorry, Britt.
- Wait.


00:40:48.484 --> 00:40:50.247
I don't need music.


00:40:51.520 --> 00:40:53.852
I love to dance and sing.


00:40:54.022 --> 00:40:55.512
BOY:
Are you kidding me?


00:40:55.991 --> 00:41:00.860
[SINGING] <i>Oh, babe, you want it like that</i>
<i>You want it like this</i>


00:41:01.763 --> 00:41:04.197
I just lose control when I'm dancing.


00:41:04.800 --> 00:41:06.631
I love it so much.


00:41:06.802 --> 00:41:08.269
<i>Oh, baby</i>


00:41:09.004 --> 00:41:10.699
Come on.


00:41:10.873 --> 00:41:12.738
What is with her?


00:41:12.908 --> 00:41:15.376
<i>Like that</i>
<i>You like it like that</i>


00:41:16.879 --> 00:41:20.406
How dare they hold that tape against you?
You were 11.


00:41:20.582 --> 00:41:24.985
What do I do? I don't want Joey to think
I'm Little Miss Stalker.


00:41:25.521 --> 00:41:27.648
You and Joey connected out there.


00:41:27.823 --> 00:41:31.122
Even if he sees the tape,
he's not gonna think you're a crazy stalker.


00:41:31.293 --> 00:41:33.022
I hope.


00:41:34.029 --> 00:41:36.224
I feel nauseous.


00:41:36.398 --> 00:41:38.457
- All right, dude?
- Yeah, fine.


00:41:44.106 --> 00:41:45.198
Whoa. Um...


00:41:45.374 --> 00:41:48.707
- Awkward.
- Ready to meet your mystery girl?


00:41:49.311 --> 00:41:51.506
Of course, you know the songs too.


00:41:51.680 --> 00:41:52.704
God, no.


00:41:52.881 --> 00:41:55.076
But I'm the real freaking one.


00:41:55.250 --> 00:41:58.549
And I freaking love you
and you just better freaking love me back...


00:41:58.720 --> 00:42:01.450
...because I'm the freaking one,
you freak.


00:42:02.157 --> 00:42:06.150
Way, way, way deep inside...


00:42:06.328 --> 00:42:08.262
...I'm sure you're a lovely person.


00:42:09.097 --> 00:42:11.088
I can prove I'm the one.


00:42:12.868 --> 00:42:14.859
Through dance.


00:42:23.212 --> 00:42:24.338
What?


00:42:24.513 --> 00:42:29.075
Okay, if this shows up on TMZ,
my attorneys will eat you all for lunch.


00:42:29.251 --> 00:42:30.548
Literally.


00:42:30.719 --> 00:42:32.550
You should talk to him.


00:42:32.721 --> 00:42:35.713
Love can bring any man... Oh, look!


00:42:35.891 --> 00:42:38.416
I'll check a couple parties.
I'll call if I get a lead.


00:42:38.594 --> 00:42:40.858
It's show time. You can do this.


00:42:42.231 --> 00:42:43.255
- I can do it.
- Yeah.


00:42:43.432 --> 00:42:44.865
Okay.


00:42:45.033 --> 00:42:48.298
- Wait, let's go get some food.
- No.


00:42:48.470 --> 00:42:50.631
I'm done with this.
There's no... Ridiculous.


00:42:50.806 --> 00:42:52.205
- Joey?
- Yeah.


00:42:52.641 --> 00:42:54.506
I have something important to tell you.


00:42:54.676 --> 00:42:57.543
- Oh, hey. You work for Dominique, right?
- What?


00:42:57.713 --> 00:43:00.045
No, no, that's...


00:43:01.083 --> 00:43:03.051
You had shrimp in your hair.


00:43:03.852 --> 00:43:07.879
Well, no. No, I mean, yes, that was me,
but that's not what I wanted to tell you.


00:43:08.056 --> 00:43:10.547
- Um, I'm...
- Dominique is relentless.


00:43:11.526 --> 00:43:13.926
Bree, Britt and now her.


00:43:14.896 --> 00:43:18.923
Look, I'm looking for somebody
and I don't have the time right now to talk.


00:43:19.101 --> 00:43:20.363
I gotta go, I'm sorry.


00:43:21.403 --> 00:43:23.268
But it was nice seeing you.


00:43:36.051 --> 00:43:37.518
Yes. Hello? Okay.


00:43:37.686 --> 00:43:40.587
Could you please connect me
to the YouTube?


00:43:42.224 --> 00:43:43.953
No, you don't understand. I have...


00:43:44.126 --> 00:43:47.061
- I told you.
- Oh, my God. He blew you off?


00:43:47.696 --> 00:43:50.756
People like me don't belong
with people like him anyway. Whatever.


00:43:52.301 --> 00:43:53.859
Damn.


00:43:56.938 --> 00:43:57.927
[INTERCOM BEEPS]


00:43:58.106 --> 00:44:01.041
DOMINIQUE: <i>Mary, I need you to</i>
<i>finalize the menu for the girls' party.</i>


00:44:01.209 --> 00:44:04.110
<i>And have Dr. Woo move up</i>
<i>my high colonic to this afternoon.</i>


00:44:04.279 --> 00:44:05.769
<i>I'm feeling blocked.</i>


00:44:05.947 --> 00:44:08.313
<i>Have your sisters' moved up too.</i>


00:44:09.584 --> 00:44:12.280
What else do I have to live for?


00:44:12.788 --> 00:44:15.518
<i>That's the spirit, sweetie.</i>


00:44:16.625 --> 00:44:18.616
[MUSIC PLAYING]


00:44:21.663 --> 00:44:23.460
[SINGING]
<i>Hold on</i>


00:44:23.632 --> 00:44:25.623
<i>Then I hear your phone a-ringing</i>


00:44:25.801 --> 00:44:29.237
<i>Just waiting for your voice to come on</i>


00:44:29.404 --> 00:44:30.769
Come on.


00:44:30.939 --> 00:44:33.066
Come on, pay attention to me.
Look at me.


00:44:33.241 --> 00:44:34.640
This is a treat for you.


00:44:34.810 --> 00:44:37.973
Oh, here. Crab cakes? Anyone?


00:44:39.781 --> 00:44:41.942
Hey. What are you doing here?


00:44:42.484 --> 00:44:43.849
Oh, I'm here to help.


00:44:44.019 --> 00:44:46.078
- I love you.
- I know.


00:44:46.254 --> 00:44:49.746
- Here. Start serving there. I'll get the rest.
- Okay.


00:44:51.426 --> 00:44:53.690
Hey, bro. Hey, bro.


00:44:53.862 --> 00:44:55.454
You want a crab cake?


00:44:56.865 --> 00:44:58.799
Yeah, man, the whole school is here.


00:44:58.967 --> 00:45:02.630
Just give me 20 minutes,
I'm gonna find your girl, all right?


00:45:03.171 --> 00:45:05.036
Gotta call you back.


00:45:05.407 --> 00:45:08.376
Hey, it's a party. Get off the phone.


00:45:10.612 --> 00:45:13.547
- Nice dance moves.
- Oh. Ha-ha-ha.


00:45:14.316 --> 00:45:17.911
You know, those purple highlights
look very familiar.


00:45:18.086 --> 00:45:22.489
You might not recognize me
without my angel wings of love.


00:45:23.125 --> 00:45:24.524
- I'm the Funk.
- The what?


00:45:24.693 --> 00:45:26.217
You know, Cupid dance.


00:45:26.395 --> 00:45:28.454
You can't forget the Cupid dance.


00:45:28.630 --> 00:45:31.224
- Oh, sorry, no. No.
- No?


00:45:31.400 --> 00:45:33.368
I'm Joey Parker's best friend.


00:45:33.535 --> 00:45:35.469
Oh. Is that supposed to impress me?


00:45:35.637 --> 00:45:38.800
Ah, you are my mystery girl. I knew it.


00:45:38.974 --> 00:45:40.202
Hey, is your friend here?


00:45:40.375 --> 00:45:42.400
What, Mary? Yeah, she's here.


00:45:42.577 --> 00:45:45.671
Can you go get her? I'm gonna call Joey.
We have to hook them up.


00:45:45.847 --> 00:45:46.871
He is in love.


00:45:47.048 --> 00:45:49.175
- Seriously? Seriously?
- Yeah. Yeah.


00:45:49.351 --> 00:45:52.514
- Awesome, I'll be right back. Okay.
- Okay.


00:45:54.156 --> 00:45:56.147
[PHONE RINGS]


00:45:57.125 --> 00:45:58.786
Dustin.


00:45:58.960 --> 00:46:01.258
- What up?
- Why does it sound like you're frowning?


00:46:01.430 --> 00:46:03.625
You better not be frowning.
What did I tell you?


00:46:03.799 --> 00:46:05.562
- What's your name?
- We're not playing...


00:46:05.734 --> 00:46:07.827
<i>We do it until you cheer up.</i>
<i>What's your name?</i>


00:46:08.003 --> 00:46:10.267
- Joey Parker.
- Who keeps it funky?


00:46:10.439 --> 00:46:12.430
- Joey Parker.
- Right. And who keeps it real?


00:46:12.607 --> 00:46:15.075
- <i>Joey Parker.</i>
- Joey Parker keeps it real, am I right?


00:46:15.243 --> 00:46:16.642
You're stupid is what you are.


00:46:16.812 --> 00:46:19.940
- Joey Parker, let me hear you screaming.
- I'm in front of her house.


00:46:20.115 --> 00:46:21.673
I know, but scream it out loud.


00:46:21.850 --> 00:46:24.216
- Joey Parker!
- <i>Joey Parker, that's right. Look.</i>


00:46:24.386 --> 00:46:27.753
All evidence indicates that your girl
is in the spot.


00:46:27.923 --> 00:46:30.221
- For real?
- <i>Your girl's inside. Come on.</i>


00:46:30.392 --> 00:46:31.882
Copy that.


00:46:33.028 --> 00:46:35.189
DOMINIQUE:
There's my girls, see?


00:46:35.764 --> 00:46:37.698
- Yeah.
- Ow!


00:46:37.866 --> 00:46:40.300
Chins up. Chins up. Tummies in.


00:46:40.469 --> 00:46:42.130
Yes.


00:46:44.473 --> 00:46:46.873
- Oh. Happy birthday.
- Thanks.


00:46:52.647 --> 00:46:55.946
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Stop right there,
Mr. Man.


00:46:56.485 --> 00:46:59.477
I'm the one, Joey Parker.


00:46:59.654 --> 00:47:00.712
So let's duet.


00:47:01.223 --> 00:47:02.588
You know, duet?


00:47:02.757 --> 00:47:04.588
You get it? Duet.


00:47:04.759 --> 00:47:06.317
Do a duet with me.


00:47:06.495 --> 00:47:09.293
Um, not if the human race
depended on it.


00:47:09.731 --> 00:47:10.823
Well, that's rude.


00:47:10.999 --> 00:47:14.230
Now, I wouldn't do a duet
with you, mister...


00:47:14.402 --> 00:47:17.030
...if we were the last two people
alive, okay?


00:47:17.205 --> 00:47:19.400
And the world was taken over by apes...


00:47:19.574 --> 00:47:22.065
...and we were the only two
with opposable thumbs...


00:47:22.244 --> 00:47:24.178
...I still wouldn't.


00:47:27.215 --> 00:47:28.239
Crab cakes?


00:47:28.416 --> 00:47:29.713
- It's fate.
- What?


00:47:29.885 --> 00:47:32.012
He's here. Now's your chance.


00:47:32.187 --> 00:47:35.156
I don't know what she's wearing.
I just know that she's here.


00:47:35.323 --> 00:47:36.950
I'm a little nervous, man.


00:47:37.125 --> 00:47:38.456
Go and talk to him.


00:47:38.627 --> 00:47:40.857
- Fine, okay, I'll go.
- Go, go, go.


00:47:41.029 --> 00:47:42.326
I hope we find her.


00:47:44.499 --> 00:47:45.523
Oh, hey.


00:47:46.268 --> 00:47:50.034
- Um... Crab cake?
- Thanks.


00:47:50.205 --> 00:47:53.766
- Can I ask you a question?
- Sure.


00:47:53.942 --> 00:47:58.174
Have you seen a girl here that can dance
like you've never seen a girl dance before?


00:47:58.346 --> 00:48:00.940
Actually, Joey, yes.


00:48:03.585 --> 00:48:06.782
- It's funny because you're looking...
MARY [ON TAPE]: <i>I love you so much, Joey.</i>


00:48:06.955 --> 00:48:08.684
<i>And you are totally kissable.</i>


00:48:08.857 --> 00:48:10.722
[CROWD LAUGHING]


00:48:10.892 --> 00:48:12.723
<i>This is for you.</i>


00:48:19.301 --> 00:48:20.325
[IMITATES CHICKEN]


00:48:20.502 --> 00:48:21.901
This can't be happening.


00:48:22.737 --> 00:48:25.570
Is that you?


00:48:26.541 --> 00:48:28.941
No, it's okay.


00:48:33.882 --> 00:48:35.873
[SOBBING]


00:48:59.774 --> 00:49:01.765
[TANGO MUSIC PLAYING]


00:49:12.020 --> 00:49:14.352
- You guys hear that?
- Yeah.


00:49:23.565 --> 00:49:24.589
Uh...


00:49:24.766 --> 00:49:26.631
I'll be right back.


00:49:26.801 --> 00:49:28.291
[GIGGLING]


00:49:38.113 --> 00:49:39.910
You're the one.


00:49:48.390 --> 00:49:50.415
I think this is yours.


00:49:54.362 --> 00:49:56.523
You tried to tell me at school too...


00:49:56.698 --> 00:49:58.791
...and I was a jerk to you.


00:50:00.101 --> 00:50:02.626
Wow, you're the one.


00:50:02.804 --> 00:50:05.671
I actually found you. This is amazing.


00:50:06.775 --> 00:50:08.208
It's cold, huh?


00:50:08.376 --> 00:50:09.400
Hey, um...


00:50:10.979 --> 00:50:13.447
- No.
- Take my jacket. No, really.


00:50:18.086 --> 00:50:20.418
You don't have to pretend
like you like me.


00:50:20.588 --> 00:50:22.647
I've had enough charity to last a lifetime.


00:50:23.291 --> 00:50:25.919
Who said anything about charity?


00:50:26.194 --> 00:50:28.822
I've been going crazy looking for you.


00:50:28.997 --> 00:50:30.624
I couldn't stop thinking about you.


00:50:31.099 --> 00:50:32.691
The way that we moved together.


00:50:34.069 --> 00:50:37.470
Well, my mom was a dancer.
So I guess it's in my blood.


00:50:41.976 --> 00:50:45.309
So you really think I'm totally kissable?


00:50:45.814 --> 00:50:47.338
What? No, that was...


00:50:48.116 --> 00:50:52.678
That was... I was a kid. I didn't... Pff. No.
Ha-ha.


00:50:53.121 --> 00:50:55.055
That's too bad. I thought it was cool.


00:50:57.459 --> 00:50:58.892
Wow, I...


00:50:59.260 --> 00:51:00.887
I know I barely know you...


00:51:01.062 --> 00:51:02.552
...but...


00:51:03.698 --> 00:51:06.189
Can I...? I wanna take you out, Mary.


00:51:07.969 --> 00:51:12.065
DOMINIQUE: Mary, get in here.
- And that's my cue.


00:51:14.209 --> 00:51:16.507
Wait, you gonna give me an answer?


00:51:17.345 --> 00:51:18.835
Yes.


00:51:23.585 --> 00:51:25.485
[ALARM BEEPING]


00:51:40.935 --> 00:51:42.425
[MARY SCREAMS]


00:51:51.312 --> 00:51:52.506
Joey.


00:51:52.680 --> 00:51:55.308
Whoa. Hey, Tony Hawk, slow down.
You know you're in a hallway.


00:51:55.483 --> 00:51:58.350
Guess who has an audition for
the Academy of Performing Arts.


00:51:58.520 --> 00:51:59.612
Me, that's who.


00:51:59.788 --> 00:52:02.552
They narrowed the applicants,
500 to 20. I'm in the top 20.


00:52:02.724 --> 00:52:05.192
Someone's gonna call, let me know
when my audition is.


00:52:05.360 --> 00:52:07.692
I'm so close I can feel it.
My gosh, Mary, breathe.


00:52:07.862 --> 00:52:10.956
- Breathe. Breathe.
- Mary, that's amazing. That's amazing.


00:52:11.132 --> 00:52:14.226
Wow. Hey, you want me to show you
some moves? Uh...


00:52:14.402 --> 00:52:16.768
For your audition.
I can help you practice.


00:52:16.938 --> 00:52:19.099
I might be into that.


00:52:19.407 --> 00:52:20.669
You might be into that?


00:52:20.842 --> 00:52:22.275
[BELL RINGS]


00:52:22.443 --> 00:52:24.104
Meet me tomorrow.


00:52:24.746 --> 00:52:26.236
[PHONE RINGING]


00:52:29.684 --> 00:52:30.708
Speak.


00:52:30.885 --> 00:52:34.821
Hello. I'm calling from the Manhattan
Academy of Performing Arts...


00:52:34.989 --> 00:52:38.390
...regarding an application
for Mary Santiago.


00:52:38.560 --> 00:52:40.585
I'm her guardian. Talk faster.


00:52:41.896 --> 00:52:43.625
We'd like to schedule an audition.


00:52:43.798 --> 00:52:46.892
Oh, no, no, no. That won't do.


00:52:47.802 --> 00:52:50.202
She can't dance.


00:52:50.371 --> 00:52:51.736
She broke both her legs.


00:52:54.175 --> 00:52:56.075
Oh, my goodness. That's awful. How?


00:52:56.244 --> 00:53:00.180
Well, they're chicken legs
and they were very weak...


00:53:00.348 --> 00:53:02.009
...and they just snapped.


00:53:02.450 --> 00:53:03.917
<i>Like twigs.</i>


00:53:04.085 --> 00:53:06.280
We'd appreciate it
if you didn't call again...


00:53:06.454 --> 00:53:12.256
...because, well, it just reminds us
that her dance career is over.


00:53:13.494 --> 00:53:15.758
Hey, I'm going clubbing in Vegas
this weekend...


00:53:15.930 --> 00:53:18.763
...you wouldn't happen to know
what the weather is like?


00:53:18.933 --> 00:53:20.264
[PHONE CLICKS]


00:53:20.435 --> 00:53:21.629
Hello?


00:53:22.370 --> 00:53:24.167
DOMINIQUE:
Hurry up and drive. I'm late.


00:53:24.339 --> 00:53:27.900
If I miss this flight, it's your fault,
you nimrod.


00:53:29.277 --> 00:53:31.905
Well, there goes the wicked witch
of the west.


00:53:32.080 --> 00:53:33.479
Maybe she took her broomstick.


00:53:33.648 --> 00:53:36.344
- You're off the hook for the weekend.
- Ha-ha-ha. Yeah.


00:53:39.721 --> 00:53:41.154
You have to be kidding me.


00:53:41.322 --> 00:53:43.381
- She's driving me nuts.
- What is it?


00:53:46.794 --> 00:53:48.625
Okay, wow. Um...


00:53:48.796 --> 00:53:50.855
"Paint the pool pink.


00:53:51.032 --> 00:53:53.227
Regrout the tile.


00:53:53.401 --> 00:53:56.928
- Vacuum the driveway"? This is ridiculous.
- Chores from Dominique.


00:53:57.105 --> 00:54:00.563
She's gone and I have to do them
or who knows how long she'll ground me.


00:54:00.742 --> 00:54:02.141
Sorry, maybe another time.


00:54:02.310 --> 00:54:04.778
Unless you do your work
while you do her work.


00:54:10.451 --> 00:54:12.112
[SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY]


00:55:07.175 --> 00:55:09.040
You're good. You are good, but I...


00:55:09.210 --> 00:55:11.770
I think we need to work on your
technique a little bit.


00:55:11.946 --> 00:55:12.970
Okay.


00:55:15.049 --> 00:55:18.314
Just, you need to loosen up
a little bit more.


00:55:19.721 --> 00:55:20.745
Not like that. No.


00:55:38.139 --> 00:55:39.163
- isn't so bad.


00:55:39.340 --> 00:55:42.332
He's doing all of her work.


00:55:42.677 --> 00:55:44.838
I feel very upset right now.


00:55:45.146 --> 00:55:46.841
Let's make her repaint the pool?


00:55:47.015 --> 00:55:52.078
Let's make her vacuum the driveway?
You're an idiot.


00:55:53.054 --> 00:55:54.783
MARY:
No. What are you doing? No.


00:55:54.956 --> 00:55:56.981
What's he see in that little freak show?


00:55:57.158 --> 00:55:59.956
Well, I think she's, like,
a good height for him.


00:56:00.128 --> 00:56:01.857
- And she has pretty hair...
- Shut up.


00:56:04.298 --> 00:56:06.129
We need a plan B.


00:56:10.104 --> 00:56:11.594
[STRING TWANGS]


00:56:12.840 --> 00:56:15.934
- Uh... I think you need a new guitar.
- Ha.


00:56:16.110 --> 00:56:18.101
Yeah, that'd be nice.


00:56:20.248 --> 00:56:22.182
You writing a new song?


00:56:23.084 --> 00:56:24.108
Yeah.


00:56:24.619 --> 00:56:26.849
You, uh, wanna help me
with the harmony?


00:56:27.889 --> 00:56:30.357
- No, I...
- I think you wanna help me with harmony.


00:56:30.525 --> 00:56:32.390
- Come on.
- Okay.


00:56:32.560 --> 00:56:34.118
Here.


00:56:35.630 --> 00:56:37.894
And this, this is as far as I got
with the lyrics.


00:56:38.066 --> 00:56:40.899
- Okay.
- Just start right here.


00:56:41.069 --> 00:56:42.400
- You ready?
- Yeah.


00:56:42.570 --> 00:56:44.197
Okay.


00:56:46.107 --> 00:56:48.701
[SINGING]
<i>It's become so hard</i>


00:56:48.876 --> 00:56:50.639
- <i>For me to be surprised</i>
- <i>For me to be surprised</i>


00:56:50.812 --> 00:56:51.836
That's good.


00:56:52.013 --> 00:56:54.777
- <i>But you're bringing back the real me</i>
- <i>But you're bringing back the real me</i>


00:56:54.949 --> 00:56:57.417
- <i>No judgment in your eyes</i>
- <i>No judgment in your eyes</i>


00:56:57.585 --> 00:57:00.452
- <i>It's the way you make me feel</i>
- <i>It's the way you make me feel</i>


00:57:00.621 --> 00:57:05.422
- <i>Like I'm finally something real</i>
- <i>Like I'm finally something real</i>


00:57:09.230 --> 00:57:10.390
Okay.


00:57:10.865 --> 00:57:12.628
Break time's over.


00:57:13.668 --> 00:57:16.136
Back to resting.


00:57:22.610 --> 00:57:24.373
[SIGHS]


00:57:24.545 --> 00:57:28.037
You know, one of the reasons I came back
was because I wanted to remember...


00:57:28.216 --> 00:57:31.151
...why I started dancing in the first place.


00:57:33.988 --> 00:57:36.013
Dancing with you...


00:57:36.757 --> 00:57:38.782
...I'm starting to remember.


00:57:41.028 --> 00:57:43.019
- Yeah?
- Yeah.


00:57:46.567 --> 00:57:48.091
And you're getting closer.


00:57:48.269 --> 00:57:49.463
So are you.


00:57:49.637 --> 00:57:53.198
- I mean with your moves.
- Well, you're not looking so bad yourself.


00:57:53.374 --> 00:57:55.569
Why don't we pick up again tomorrow,
right here?


00:57:55.743 --> 00:57:57.973
As in my house, as in this position?


00:57:58.146 --> 00:57:59.340
I'm not that kind of guy.


00:57:59.514 --> 00:58:02.483
Somehow I don't find that
entirely convincing.


00:58:09.891 --> 00:58:12.189
So where's Prince Charming now?


00:58:12.360 --> 00:58:15.329
Couldn't stand to spend another second
with his charity case?


00:58:15.496 --> 00:58:17.396
Wow, jealous much?


00:58:17.565 --> 00:58:18.759
[DOORBELL RINGS]


00:58:18.933 --> 00:58:22.664
Was that the doorbell? That's strange.
I wonder who that could be.


00:58:22.837 --> 00:58:25.499
I don't know, Bree.
Get that, would you, Mary?


00:58:25.673 --> 00:58:27.140
God, you guys are weird.


00:58:30.077 --> 00:58:32.443
Hello, plan B.


00:58:32.613 --> 00:58:34.342
Could you be more obvious?


00:58:34.515 --> 00:58:37.143
Well, no. That would totally give it away.


00:58:53.768 --> 00:58:55.292
Tami, what if he fell asleep?


00:58:55.469 --> 00:58:58.165
No way. Go. And call me later.


00:58:58.339 --> 00:59:00.705
Domifreak took my cell phone,
remember?


00:59:00.875 --> 00:59:02.672
Do you want me to wait?


00:59:02.977 --> 00:59:05.810
No, I'm good. Joey will take me home.
Thank you.


00:59:05.980 --> 00:59:07.971
- Go kill it.
- Okay.


00:59:22.630 --> 00:59:24.393
[SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY]


00:59:32.907 --> 00:59:34.397
[GATE CLANGS]


00:59:38.713 --> 00:59:40.305
What was that?


00:59:40.748 --> 00:59:42.511
- What's going on?
- Nothing.


00:59:42.683 --> 00:59:45.413
Natalia. Natalia, look. Ha.


00:59:45.586 --> 00:59:47.986
We had a thing, but it's over.


00:59:48.923 --> 00:59:51.915
- Joey. Joey, come on.
- It's time for you to go.


00:59:52.093 --> 00:59:53.822
I'll see you at school.


01:00:25.726 --> 01:00:27.717
[SNORING]


01:00:27.895 --> 01:00:30.455
Hey, where have you been all night?


01:00:30.631 --> 01:00:33.532
I'm just doing a little yoga.


01:00:35.536 --> 01:00:39.404
Hey, have you been crying?
Or are you just naturally puffy?


01:00:39.573 --> 01:00:42.041
I never noticed that before.
What's wrong?


01:00:42.209 --> 01:00:45.042
- Dominique, I'd rather not talk about it.
- Oh, come on.


01:00:45.212 --> 01:00:47.146
Talk to me. Come on, sit down.


01:00:47.815 --> 01:00:50.477
Come on, sit down. Come on.


01:00:51.185 --> 01:00:52.652
Okay. Sit in the hand.


01:00:53.688 --> 01:00:55.747
Is it Joey, honey?


01:00:55.923 --> 01:00:58.551
Oh, I knew it.


01:00:58.726 --> 01:01:02.059
Did he find someone prettier
and more successful?


01:01:02.229 --> 01:01:05.392
Oh, I'm sorry. That is difficult.


01:01:05.566 --> 01:01:09.093
Not that I would know, but I did take
an acting class once. I can imagine.


01:01:09.970 --> 01:01:14.134
Let me give you a word of advice.
Joey is an <i>E! Hollywood True Story...</i>


01:01:14.308 --> 01:01:16.674
...just waiting to happen.


01:01:16.844 --> 01:01:19.438
There's no sense crying over him.
Mm-mm.


01:01:19.613 --> 01:01:22.104
In fact, it's kind of pathetic.


01:01:23.050 --> 01:01:25.518
I can't wait to get out of here
and move to Manhattan.


01:01:25.686 --> 01:01:29.087
Oh, I'm sorry. Did I forget to tell you?
I did, my bad.


01:01:29.256 --> 01:01:32.248
They called. There's no audition.
It was a mistake.


01:01:32.426 --> 01:01:35.259
- What? You're lying.
- No, I'm not.


01:01:35.429 --> 01:01:37.829
The rejection letter is right there
in that mess...


01:01:37.998 --> 01:01:41.365
...you need to clean up here
and sort through.


01:01:44.739 --> 01:01:46.639
I'm so glad we had this little talk.


01:01:46.807 --> 01:01:51.244
I've always wanted to be the mother
you'll never have.


01:01:54.548 --> 01:01:58.609
Yeah. So the Japan tour was awesome.
Like a Bruce Lee movie, but no subtitles.


01:01:58.786 --> 01:02:01.653
- The sushi kind of made me sick...
- Mary.


01:02:02.656 --> 01:02:05.056
Hey. Catch you in a minute.


01:02:05.226 --> 01:02:06.750
Mary.


01:02:07.428 --> 01:02:10.397
Mary, slow down. Hey, what...?


01:02:10.564 --> 01:02:11.724
What's wrong?


01:02:11.899 --> 01:02:14.424
I've been calling Tami,
trying to get ahold of you.


01:02:16.504 --> 01:02:19.166
- What did I do?
- It doesn't matter. It's done. We're done.


01:02:20.408 --> 01:02:21.807
Wait.


01:02:22.176 --> 01:02:23.666
Whoa, whoa.


01:02:23.844 --> 01:02:26.404
- What are you talking about?
- Did you feel sorry for me?


01:02:26.580 --> 01:02:29.048
Was I your charity case?
Is that why you asked me out?


01:02:29.216 --> 01:02:31.878
- What does that mean?
- You figured you'd toy with me...


01:02:32.052 --> 01:02:34.680
...until someone better came along
and I wouldn't mind...


01:02:34.855 --> 01:02:36.846
...because I was lucky
a big star wanted me.


01:02:37.124 --> 01:02:41.458
You know what really sucks about falling
for a guy you know you're not right for?


01:02:42.029 --> 01:02:45.624
You fall anyway because you think
he might turn out to be different.


01:02:46.333 --> 01:02:47.766
Mary.


01:02:49.737 --> 01:02:51.170
- I am different.
- Anyway...


01:02:51.338 --> 01:02:54.000
...thanks for all the dance moves,
but I'm done dancing.


01:02:54.175 --> 01:02:55.665
Goodbye.


01:02:58.078 --> 01:03:00.342
DUSTIN:
All right, time for some damage control.


01:03:00.514 --> 01:03:03.574
And what'd I tell you? My mystery girl.


01:03:08.322 --> 01:03:10.119
- Whoa, Tami.
- I need your help.


01:03:10.291 --> 01:03:12.259
- What's with the blinds?
- It's about Mary.


01:03:12.426 --> 01:03:15.122
- Come on, girl.
- Don't you "girl" me.


01:03:15.896 --> 01:03:18.091
Just give me a second.


01:03:18.265 --> 01:03:19.289
One second.


01:03:19.467 --> 01:03:22.630
Don't you have a stadium show to play
or something?


01:03:22.803 --> 01:03:24.065
Come on. Back door.


01:03:25.873 --> 01:03:27.238
